proposed_statement_changes.proposed:
Put \(A_{n,m,\tau}:=\ell\min\{1,N^{-\varkappa}\}\) and \(L_m:=\log(2m)\). Restrict the unresolved regret problem to the strict sub-familywise phase
\[
A_{n,m,\tau}<L_m^{1-\varkappa}.                                       \tag{56}
\]
In this phase the proved bracket is
\[
c_{\beta,D}\min\!\left\{\ell,
A_{n,m,\tau}\left[1+A_{n,m,\tau}^{\varkappa/(1-\varkappa)}\right]\right\}
\leq\mathcal R(n,m,\tau)
\leq C_{\beta,D}\min\{\ell,A_{n,m,\tau}L_m^{\varkappa}\}
=C_{\beta,D}\mathcal B_{\mathrm{CK}}(n,m,\tau).                       \tag{57}
\]
Determine \(\mathcal R(n,m,\tau)\) up to constants depending only on \(\beta,D\) within (56). In particular, construct one computable capacity-aware learner over the full heterogeneous class \(\mathcal H_{\beta,D}(m)\) that attains the lower expression in (57), including sparse-dominance, collective-contribution, and local-to-tied mixtures, or prove that another same-class configuration raises the lower bound. Determine whether \(A_{n,m,\tau}\to0\), which is necessary for vanishing regret, is sufficient, or whether the stronger currently sufficient condition \(A_{n,m,\tau}L_m^{\varkappa}\to0\) is necessary. Equivalently, identify the maximal subregimes of (56) on which capacity averaging yields \(\mathcal R(n,m,\tau)=o\{\mathcal B_{\mathrm{CK}}(n,m,\tau)\}\). The existing coordinatewise learner \(\widehat\pi_{\mathrm{tail}}\) remains only the upper witness in (57); no nonzero policy-selection price is assumed.

